  "limitations": [
    "Shared-host non-isolated runs establish no causal speed-up or production latency; concurrent owned scoped test/build work and other uncharacterised host load were not removed.",
    "Native and absent environments use different NumPy versions; recorded current results are checked for projection correctness and identical actual input hashes, not a controlled cross-version performance experiment.",
    "Python public projection times include Python source validation/constraint calls; PyO3 calls include sequence extraction/output conversion; Rust iter_batched keeps raw clone setup outside its interval but includes returned-buffer handling. These are different entry-point costs.",
    "Historical 2026-09-26 construction/projection snapshot used different inputs and toolchains; historical Criterion first local projection run also used inputs unlike then-current Python RNG sample. Both remain historical evidence, not current-head or isolated baselines.",
    "Empty/extreme structural projection does not guarantee stable physical dynamics under every possible coupling magnitude.",
    "No Go/Julia/Mojo counterpart for this fixed K_nm projection was found in maintained native source directories. No global coverage or Rust instruction100 claim.",
    "Initial v3 Python timing collection ran under coverage and was retained verbatim internally as instrumented evidence; current v4 raw receipts replace those timings with independent uninstrumented runs."
